  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Building Legal Aid Movement Resilience to Strengthen Rule of Law, Human Rights, and Democracy</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This proposed FCDO-to-Indonesian people collaboration seeks to support Indonesia&#x2019;s good practices through supporting a series of initiatives, including to establish anti-criminalisation center, training paramedia , and civil society consolidation by strengthening Democratic League. This proposal is part of a larger effort in project Strengthening the Rule of Law and Reverse the Regression of Democracy and Human Rights by Revitalizing the Structural Legal Aid Movement funded by Embassy of the Kingdom of the Netherlands. Project funded by Embassy of the Kingdom of the Netherlands shall fund these initiatives in 15 LBH while this proposed project will fund 3 in key areas of Bali, Medan, and Jakarta. The project seeks to enhance human rights defenders (HRDs) protection through increasing legal aid organizations&#x2019; capacity to provide better legal aid for HRDS as the host of the Anti-Criminalisation Center in their respective province, supporting pro-human rights and rule of law activism and grassroots organizations through capacity building for legal aid lawyers and community-based paramedia and consolidating civil society movements in advocating the strengthening of democracy, rule of law, and human rights by strengthening the Democratic League</narrative>
  </description>
